 "answer": "I can't pull a verified live reading, and the pages I found are snapshots from different times. Together they suggest Penang's air quality is **moderate**, with PM2.5 the main pollutant.\n\n| Source | AQI | Category |\n|---|---|---|\n| Weather Underground (Penang) | 68 | Moderate |\n| AccuWeather (Penang Airport) | 67 | AccuWeather labels this \"Poor\" |\n| IQAir (Bukit Mertajam) | 58 | Moderate |\n| IQAir (George Town) | 125 | Unhealthy for sensitive groups |\n| IQAir (Tanjung Tokong) | 79 | Moderate |\n| IQAir (Batu Feringgi) | 159 | Unhealthy |\n\n- **Timing:** The IQAir pages are stamped with different dates in October, and one search result was marked as 114 days old. Some of these numbers are stale.\n- **Variation:** Readings differ by location and over the day. PM2.5 can spike, for example during regional haze or traffic peaks.\n- **Labels:** AccuWeather uses its own scale, so its label differs from the US AQI scale for a similar number.\n\nSensitive groups, such as people with asthma, heart or lung conditions, children and older adults, should limit prolonged outdoor exertion when AQI is above about 50 to 100.\n\nFor a real-time figure, check these pages directly:\n- IQAir's George Town page: https://www.iqair.com/air-quality/malaysia/penang/george-town\n- Malaysia's DOE Air Pollutant Index (API) at apims.doe.gov.my",
